<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- edited with XMLSpy v2008 rel. 2 (http://www.altova.com) by EPO User (Europäisches Patentamt) -->
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" version="0.2">
	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>This version of the schema has been designed to cater for the exchange of data extracted from INPADOC, the EPO's master database for Worldwide Legal Status.
			It has been tailored to support legacy data that dates back to the early days of the database.
			With a view to the historic significance of legal status data and the need to be able to exchange back-file data, it will have to able to support legacy data into the future
			This database specific version of the schema will comply with the international standard for the exchange of legal status database where possible and use product-specific tags where necessary.
			Further information in document T03.03_User Documentation Legstat_XML, authored by Fenny Versloot-Spoelstra, available on-line under link http://www.epo.org/searching/data/data/manuals.html
		</xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>
	<!--
*******************************************************************************************
AMENDMENTS
20140916_Version [legal-status-documents-v0-5-10-3-transional
attribute "family-id" @ element [application-reference] from "required" to "optional"
attribute "date-added" @ element [legal-event] from "required" to "optional"
attributes "status", "sequence" new @ elements [fee-payment], [notification-of-lapse], [notification-of-reinstatement], [patent-classification] and [parties]
20150701_Version legal-status-documents-v1-0-transional
Version-nummers increased to 1.0 with migration to production
20160101_Version legal-status-documents-v1-1-transional
Concept of "grouped event" has been abandoned:
Impact on structure of <event-details>:
<fee-payments> now <fee-payment>
<notifications-of-lapse> now <notification-of-lapse>
<notifications-of-reinstatement> now <notification-of-reinstatement>
<patent-classifications> no <patent-classification>
2016/March_Version legal-status-documents-v1-2-transional
Restriction base of DateType simplified to overcome legacy issues
Removed identity constraint on publication-reference
Element <fee-payment> - choice between <fee-payment-year> only or <fee-payment-date> only or both <fee-payment-year> and <fee-payment-date>
Element <parties> - attribute "party-type" - value "applicant" now "licensee"
2016/March_Version legal-status-documents-v1-2-1-transional
Element <publication-reference> - minOccurs="0" - will not always be supported when <legal-status-document status="D">
2016/March_Version legal-status-documents-v1-2-2-transional
Element <event-document> replaced by new element <event-reference> offering a choice:
element <event-ref-document> - previously <event-document> - reference to a patent by means of a document-number
element <event-ref-kind> - previously <reference-to-publication> - reference to a patent by means of a document kind-code
2016/May_Version legal-status-documents-v1-2-3-transional
Element <event-document> replaced by new element <event-reference> offering an additional choice:
element <event-ref-document> - previously <event-document> - reference to a patent by means of a document-number
element <event-ref-kind> - previously <reference-to-publication> - reference to a patent by means of a document kind-code
element <text> - populated with the information available when some of the elements required are missing
Element <fee-payment-year>
restriction increased to 40 years
Element <parties-details-old> not populated anymore
previous owners and other additional information exchanged in <parties><text>
2017/Feb_Version legal-status-documents-v-1-2-4
Element <date-filing> now both child element in <event-details> and in <spc>
only populated in <spc> when there are other spc elements available as well
2017/July_Version legal-status-documents-v-1-2-5
New attribute “event-id” at legal-event – defined “optional” – representing the unique and stable identifier to the legal event:
In the case of a deleted event – status=”D” @ legal-event - identifier allows to pinpoint the exact event to delete
In the case of an updated event – status=”D” on before image + status=”C” on after image - identifier allows to pair up before and after image of one and the same event
2020/Jan_Version legal-status-documents-v-1-2-6
New attribute “sequence-number” at element <party> – defined “optional”
2020/Jul_Version legal-status-documents-v-1-2-7
Element <address> - element <country> replaced by element <state-country> to allow for codes identifying states within the USA
2020/Oct_Version legal-status-documents-v-1-2-8
Set date-patent-lapsed not  a mandatory field
*******************************************************************************************-->
	<!--
*******************************************************************************************
 IMPORTED NAMESPACES
*******************************************************************************************-->
	<xs:import namespace="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"/>
	<!--
*******************************************************************************************
 ROOT ELEMENTS
*******************************************************************************************-->
	<xs:element name="legal-status-documents" type="LegalStatusDocumentsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
				This element is the "super-root".
				It is the wrapper for one or more instances of "legal-status-document".
				Each instance of "legal-status-document" represents an application in INPADOC, the master database for the EPO worldwide legal status data
			</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="legal-status-document" type="LegalStatusDocumentType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
				This element is the "root".
				It represents one application in INPADOC, the master database for worldwide legal status
				It is the wrapper for one or more instances of "legal-event".
			</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<!--
		<xs:key name="PublicationReferenceKey">
			<xs:selector xpath="publication-reference"/>
			<xs:field xpath="document-id/kind"/>
		</xs:key>

		<xs:keyref name="PublicationReferenceKeyRef" refer="PublicationReferenceKey">
			<xs:selector xpath="legal-event"/>
			<xs:field xpath="@reference-to-publication"/>
		</xs:keyref>
		-->
		<xs:unique name="SequenceNumberKey">
			<xs:selector xpath="legal-event"/>
			<xs:field xpath="@sequence-number"/>
		</xs:unique>
	</xs:element>
	<!--
*******************************************************************************************
 ELEMENTS
*******************************************************************************************-->
	<xs:element name="address">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ST.36 unstructured address.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="address-1" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element name="address-2" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element name="address-3" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element name="address-4" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element name="address-5" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element ref="state-country"/>
			</xs:sequence>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="application-reference" type="DocumentReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Application reference information: application number, country
				.
				In case of a filing refererence, the kind code is empty and the date refers to
				the filing date
				.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="country" type="ST3HistoryCountryCodeType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ST.3 country code, also includes EP and WO. Uppercase always.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="state-country" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Allows codes identifying states within the USA</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="date" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Date: components of a date. Format ISO8601 short: YYYYMMDD.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-date-effective" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The date that the legal event has come into force.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="date-expiry-of-patent" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The date that the original underlying patent to the SPC expires or has expired.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="date-filing" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L512EP</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="date-extension-granted" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The date that extension of terms has been granted.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="date-application-withdrawn" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The date that the application has been withdrawn.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="doc-number" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Serial number of the referenced patent (or application) document.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="document-id">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Document identification refers to patents
				(and patent applications) only.
				See WIPO ST.14.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element ref="country"/>
				<xs:element ref="doc-number"/>
				<xs:element ref="kind" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element ref="name" minOccurs="0"/>
				<xs:element ref="date" minOccurs="0"/>
			</xs:sequence>
			<xs:attribute name="document-id-type" use="optional">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>not supported in this product</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
						<xs:enumeration value="docdb"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="epodoc"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="original"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:attribute>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-class" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Event Class - when populated - represents the INPADOC classification allocated by the EPO</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-code" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Event code as provided by the generating office.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-date" type="DateType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Date of the event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-description">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Textual description (localized) of the event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:simpleContent>
				<xs:extension base="xs:string">
					<xs:attribute name="event-description-type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>
								Value "original" identifies the description as originally supplied by the national authority.
							</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
						<xs:simpleType>
							<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
								<xs:enumeration value="original"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="translation"/>
							</xs:restriction>
						</xs:simpleType>
					</xs:attribute>
					<xs:attribute name="lang" type="ISO639-1LanguageCode">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>
								Value "en" identifies the description in the English language; this may the the original description or a translation.
							</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:attribute>
				</xs:extension>
			</xs:simpleContent>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-details" type="EventDetailsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Grouping element for the details of an event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="gazette-reference">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Information about an office's gazette or bulletin - paper, electronic, etc.
				where, the details of the patent publication are also given.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="gazette-num" type="xs:string"/>
				<xs:element ref="date"/>
				<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0"/>
			</xs:sequence>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="kind" type="KindType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Document kind code; e.g., A1</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="legal-event" type="LegalEventType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>
				Represents one legal event in INPADOC, the master database for worldwide legal status
			</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="name" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Name of a person or entity.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="party" type="PartyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Grouping element identifying a party in the proceedings.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="fee-payment">
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:choice maxOccurs="2">
					<xs:element name="fee-payment-date" type="DateType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L518EP</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="fee-payment-year">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Eg. "4", "8", "10", "15", ...; reference to legacy product: L520EP</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
						<xs:simpleType>
							<xs:restriction base="xs:positiveInteger">
								<xs:maxInclusive value="40"/>
							</xs:restriction>
						</xs:simpleType>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:choice>
				<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L510EP</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
			</xs:sequence>
			<xs:attribute ref="country"/>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="notification-of-lapse">
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="date-patent-lapsed" type="DateType" minOccurs="0">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L525EP when code="PG25"</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0"/>
			</xs:sequence>
			<xs:attribute ref="country"/>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="notification-of-reinstatement">
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="date-patent-reinstated" type="DateType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L525EP when code="PGRI"</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0"/>
			</xs:sequence>
			<xs:attribute ref="country"/>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="patent-classification">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element will only ever contain IPC classifications, either IPC1/7 or IPC/8; fdefinition has been reduced to "classification-symbol" unstructured; reference to legacy product: L516EP</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexType>
			<xs:sequence>
				<xs:element name="classification-scheme">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>This elements allows to identify the classification scheme and the corresponding edition or validity date.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
					<xs:complexType>
						<xs:choice minOccurs="0">
							<xs:element name="edition"/>
							<xs:element ref="date"/>
						</xs:choice>
						<xs:attribute name="office" type="ST3HistoryCountryCodeType" use="optional">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>ST.3 code of the office maintainning the classification scheme, e.g., for IPC use WO.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:attribute>
						<xs:attribute name="scheme" use="required">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Name of the scheme, e.g., IPC8</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:attribute>
					</xs:complexType>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="classification-symbol" type="xs:string">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Classification symbol in an unstructured format.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
			</xs:sequence>
		</xs:complexType>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="product" type="ProductType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Grouping tag for an SPC product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="publication-reference" type="DocumentReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Publication reference information: publication number, date, etc</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="registration" type="RegistrationType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Registration information of a product (SPC).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="spc" type="SPCType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Grouping tag for SPC information.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-reference" type="EventReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Grouping tag for reference to a patent document</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-ref-document" type="EventRefDocumentType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Refers to a patent document by means of a document-number. Note that indication whether publication or application is not supported
				L504EP - country
				L503EP - doc-number
				L506EP - kind
				L505EP - date		</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="event-ref-kind" type="EventRefKindType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Refers to a patent document by means of a reference to the kind-code. Note that indication whether publication or application is not supported
				L506EP - kind
				L505EP - date		</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="text" type="xs:string">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Text field. In a choice to be used when no other possibility to capture the information; reference to legacy product: L510EP</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<!--
*******************************************************************************************
 COMPLEX TYPES
*******************************************************************************************-->
	<xs:complexType name="DocumentReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type to describe a container for a set of document identifications.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="document-id" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute ref="doc-id" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Provides a unique and stable link to the corresponding application in DOCDB
					Allows for mixing and matching data between EPO raw data products "INPADOC Worldwide Legal Status" and "EPO Patent Information Resource" (DOCDB/XML)		</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="lang" type="ISO639-1LanguageCode" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L514EP
					Only populated when attributed to "publication-reference"</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EventDetailsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the details of a legal event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="event-description" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Describes the detailed nature of the event defined by element "event-code". This element is further identified by either attribute "event-description-type" or attribute "lang".
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="event-reference" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Refers to a patent document by means of a document-number or a document kind-code. Note that indication whether publication or application is not supported
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="date-application-withdrawn" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the date of withdrawal. Reference to legacy product: L526EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="date-filing" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L512EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="parties" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>One instance of "parties" will contain: one occurrence of "party" for each current owner, representative etc. One instance of parties may contain one occurrence of "text" containing the previous owner(s), representative(s) etc, concatenated into one string of freetext. Element is further identified by attribute "party-type". Values with reference to the legacy product :
						L509EP - owner
						L517EP - representative
						L515EP - inventor
						L519EP - opponent
						L522EP - licensee					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element name="parties-details">
							<xs:complexType>
								<xs:sequence>
									<xs:element ref="party" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
								</xs:sequence>
							</xs:complexType>
							<xs:unique name="PartySequenceNumberKey">
								<xs:selector xpath="party"/>
								<xs:field xpath="@sequence-number"/>
							</xs:unique>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element name="parties-details-old" minOccurs="0">
							<xs:complexType>
								<xs:choice>
									<xs:element ref="party" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
									<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0">
										<xs:annotation>
											<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L510EP</xs:documentation>
										</xs:annotation>
									</xs:element>
								</xs:choice>
							</xs:complexType>
							<xs:unique name="PartyOldSequenceNumberKey">
								<xs:selector xpath="party"/>
								<xs:field xpath="@sequence-number"/>
							</xs:unique>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>for US assignments : conveyance text</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:sequence>
					<xs:attribute name="party-type" use="required">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This product supports : owner, representative, licensee, inventor, opponent</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
						<xs:simpleType>
							<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
								<xs:enumeration value="owner"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="representative"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="licensee"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="inventor"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="applicant"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="applicant-inventor"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="opponent"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="third-party"/>
								<xs:enumeration value="other"/>
							</xs:restriction>
						</xs:simpleType>
					</xs:attribute>
					<xs:attribute ref="status"/>
					<xs:attribute ref="sequence-number"/>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="spc" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Supplementary Protection Certificate</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="designated-states" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L507EP; parsed into one occurence of "country" for each designated country</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element ref="country" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="extension-states" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L508EP; parsed into one occurence of "country" for each extension state</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:sequence>
						<xs:element ref="country" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
					</xs:sequence>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="fee-payment" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Fee payment event for a country.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="notification-of-lapse" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Notification of lapse for a country.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="notification-of-reinstatement" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Notification of reinstatement for a country.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="patent-classification" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element ref="text" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Catering for events that are not supported by any of the above elements; reference to legacy product: L510EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="LegalEventType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the descripton of a legal event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="event-date">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the date this event was made available to the public, in gazette or on-line Reference to legacy product: L007EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="event-date-effective" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the date this event has come into force
						Reference to legacy product: L525EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="gazette-reference" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to the gazette in which this event was published.
						Currently not supported by the database, included for potential future use</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="event-class" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element ref="event-code">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the detailed country-specific nature of the event; reference to legacy product: if   L008EP not = REG then L008EP; if   L008EP = REG then L502EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="event-details"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="event-type" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Attribute event-type="REG" identifies that the event has bearing on a national application based on a regional filing; reference to legacy product: if L008EP="REG" then value "REG"</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
					<xs:enumeration value="REG"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="providing-office" type="ST3HistoryCountryCodeType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Attribute "providing-office" identifies the national office that has provided the event; reference to legacy product: if L008EP="REG" then L501EP else L001EP; if PCT filing (kind-code="W") then "WO" instead of L001EP	</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="event-id" type="ElementIdentifier">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Unique and stable identifier to the legal event </xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute ref="status"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="date-added"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="date-previous-exchange"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="sequence-number" use="required"/>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="LegalStatusDocumentsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the bulk exchange of Legal Status Documents.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="legal-status-document" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="date-produced" type="DateType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Represents date of database extraction.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="date-of-exchange" type="DateType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Represents date of making data available to 3rd parties.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="schema-version" type="xs:string" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Refers to version of the schema used to produce this instance. </xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="file" type="xs:string" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Refers to the packaging-file containing this instance</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="number-of-documents" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Represents number of legal status documents contained in this instance.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:integer">
					<xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="generating-office" type="ST3HistoryCountryCodeType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>ST.3 code representing the office generating this instance</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="complete-history" type="xs:boolean" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Value 'true' represents "complete history" and identifies "back-file", i.e. each application is provided with all of its legal events. Value 'false' represents "updates only" and identifies "front-file"
				</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="LegalStatusDocumentType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type describing a legal status document, i.e., the legal status information about a single patent document.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="application-reference">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The application-reference is the key-identifier to the set of legal events; reference to legacy product: L001EP - country, L003EP - doc-number, L014EP - date</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="publication-reference" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element contains all publications available in the DOCDB, the master database for patent bibliographic data; reference to legacy product: L017EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ipr-type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This product supports "patent for invention" and "utility model" only; reference to legacy product: L005EP [ WIPO ST.17 Part B(ii) ]	</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:enumeration value="patent for invention"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="patent of addition"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="patent of improvement"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="patent of importation"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="plant patent"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="inventor's certificate"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="inventor's certificate of addition"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="utility certificate"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="utility certificate of additon"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="utility model"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="design"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="industrial model"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="other"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ipr-status" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Currently not supported in this product [ WIPO ST.17 Part B(ii) ]
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:pattern value="[12349]"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="legal-event" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents one legal event in INPADOC, the EPO master database for worldwide legal status.	</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute ref="family-id"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="status"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="date-added"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="date-previous-exchange"/>
		<xs:attribute ref="country" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Populated with application country-code, for PCT applications with "WO"
					Reference to legacy product: L001EP; if PCT filing (kind="W") then "WO" instead of L001EP.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="number-of-events" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Represents number of legal status events contained in this instance.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:integer">
					<xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PartyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the description of a party to the proceedings.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="name">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Element "name" may contain address data, concatenated and separated by , or ;	</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="execution-date" type="DateType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>for US assignments : execution-date transfer of ownership</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="address" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Currently not supported. When data available, then country of residence only	</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute ref="sequence-number"/>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ProductType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the description of a product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="name"/>
			<xs:element ref="registration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RegistrationType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type for the description the registration of a product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="country"/>
			<xs:element name="registration-number" type="xs:string"/>
			<xs:element name="registration-date" type="DateType"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="registration-level" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Value "national" identifies "registration in the country of the national office"; value "regional" identifies "first registration in a country within the economic area"</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
					<xs:enumeration value="national"/>
					<xs:enumeration value="regional"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="region-name" type="xs:string">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>"EEA" - European Economic Area</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SPCType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Type to describe a SPC. The content of this element is highly variable.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="spc-number" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L511EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="date-filing" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L512EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="date-expiry-of-patent" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the date the original underlying patent has expired; reference to legacy product: L513EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="date-extension-granted" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the date extension of terms have been granted; reference to legacy product: L523EP</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:choice minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
						Currently information on product and product registration is stored in the master database in a blob of freetext.
						The contents of this blob of freetext is too volatile and complex to parse at exchange time.
						It is the intention to capture and record this information in dedicated tags in the future.
						Until such time information on product and product registration will be included and exchanged as freetext in "text"
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:element ref="product"/>
				<xs:element ref="text">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Reference to legacy product: L510EP</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
			</xs:choice>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EventReferenceType">
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element ref="event-ref-document"/>
			<xs:element ref="event-ref-kind"/>
			<xs:element ref="text">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Populated when some of the elements required are not available</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EventRefDocumentType">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="country"/>
			<xs:element ref="doc-number"/>
			<xs:element ref="kind" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element ref="name" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element ref="date" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="document-id-type" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>not supported in this product</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
					<xs:enumeration value="docdb"/>
					<xs:enumeration value="epodoc"/>
					<xs:enumeration value="original"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EventRefKindType">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="kind"/>
			<xs:element ref="date" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
